    {
      "_id": "OK9v4kEpgOSW95Kh",
      "name": "Voremind Traits",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "systems/pf1/icons/skills/blood_04.jpg",
      "effects": [],
      "folder": null,
      "sort": 30000,
      "flags": {
        "core": {},
        "pf1": {
          "migration": "11.11"
        }
      },
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<h2>The Voremind</h2><p>The Voremind are not creatures of death. They are life stripped of individuality, a biological consciousness that views all living things as incomplete pieces of itself.</p><p>Unlike the undead, the Voremind do not raise corpses through necromancy. They consume and reconstruct organic material, weaving living tissue into entirely new organisms.</p><p>Their most terrifying trait is that they keep the memories of the creatures they assimilate. As their numbers grow, so does their collective intelligence.</p><p>Ancient scholars of the Grand Archive called the outbreak <em>the Carrion Bloom</em>. They believed they were containing a disease. What they actually imprisoned was an intelligent species.</p><p>Every Voremind creature is a living aberration, not undead. Positive energy heals it. Negative energy harms it. Undead-only effects, including channel energy against undead, do not treat it as undead. It is immune to Assimilating Blight and not immune to other diseases. It can be critically hit, sneaked, poisoned, and affected by mind-affecting effects unless a statblock says otherwise.</p>\n<p><strong>Assimilating Blight</strong> is an extraordinary biological disease. Injury or inhaled, as the attack says. Onset 1 round, frequency 1/round for 6 rounds, 1d2 Constitution and 1d2 Wisdom damage, sickened for 1 round on a failed save, cure 2 consecutive saves. A creature that dies infected, or whose Constitution or Wisdom reaches 0 from the disease, becomes one of the Reclaimed after 1d4 rounds if the body is intact. <em>Remove disease</em> or <em>heal</em> ends the blight before that change. After the change, the creature is a new aberration.</p>",
          "instructions": "",
          "unidentified": ""
        },
