        }
      },
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>Standard action melee touch. On a hit the parasite attaches and occupies the target's space without grappling. This attack does not provoke. At the start of the parasite's next turn, if it is still attached, the target saves Fortitude DC 12 against Assimilating Blight and this creature merges into the victim and is destroyed as a separate creature.</p><p>Removing it is a standard action and a DC 12 Strength or Escape Artist check by the victim or an adjacent ally. Any damage to the attached parasite also detaches it. Swarming instinct: +1 on the attack if the target already has another Fleshseed attached.</p>",
          "instructions": "",
          "unidentified": ""
        },
