    "details": {
      "height": "",
      "weight": "",
      "gender": "",
      "deity": "",
      "age": "",
      "alignment": "n",
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>A bulbous parasite with whipping tendrils. It leaps, latches, and burrows.</em></p><p><strong>Fleshseed</strong> — CR 1, XP 400.</p><h2>Conduct</h2><p>It wants the wounded, the isolated, and the helpless. A group comes from several directions at once.</p><h2>Species</h2><p>Every Voremind creature is a living aberration, not undead. Positive energy heals it. Negative energy harms it. Undead-only effects, including channel energy against undead, do not treat it as undead. It is immune to Assimilating Blight and not immune to other diseases. It can be critically hit, sneaked, poisoned, and affected by mind-affecting effects unless a statblock says otherwise.</p>\n<p><strong>Assimilating Blight</strong> is an extraordinary biological disease. Injury or inhaled, as the attack says. Onset 1 round, frequency 1/round for 6 rounds, 1d2 Constitution and 1d2 Wisdom damage, sickened for 1 round on a failed save, cure 2 consecutive saves. A creature that dies infected, or whose Constitution or Wisdom reaches 0 from the disease, becomes one of the Reclaimed after 1d4 rounds if the body is intact. <em>Remove disease</em> or <em>heal</em> ends the blight before that change. After the change, the creature is a new aberration.</p><p>Voremind within 300 feet share what any one of them has perceived. They know the location, not line of sight, and they do not ignore concealment.</p><p>Fire and acid do not bypass its defenses. On a form with fast healing, either damage type suppresses that healing until the end of its next turn.</p>"
      },
